<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<model version="NetLogo 7.0.4" snapToGrid="false">
  <code>;; Team knowledge emergence: Grand, J. A., Braun, M. T., Kuljanin, G., Kozlowski, S. W. J.,
;; &amp; Chao, G. T. (2016). The dynamics of team cognition: A process-oriented theory of knowledge
;; emergence in teams. Journal of Applied Psychology, 101(10), 1353-1385.
;; Follows Table A1/A2 and the authors' supplementary R code (APL-2014-0766R3_Supp.R.txt):
;; 3 agents; 36 data pieces (common + unique per agent); information = integrated PAIRS of
;; data of the same type; 50-step learning and sharing phases; encoding 3-5 / 6-8 / 9-11
;; repetitions; decoding = encoding + 1; each integration takes one step.
;; Speaking probabilities follow the paper (favored member twice as likely: 50/25/25).
globals [ n-common n-uniq pairs owner phase clock done-at ]
turtles-own [ enc dec speak dprog order info said ]

to setup
  clear-all
  set n-uniq (ifelse-value specialization = "low (33% unique)" [ 4 ] specialization = "moderate (50% unique)" [ 6 ] [ 8 ])
  set n-common 36 - 3 * n-uniq
  set pairs [] set owner []
  foreach range n-common [ i -&gt; foreach range i [ j -&gt; set pairs lput (list j i) pairs set owner lput -1 owner ] ]
  foreach range 3 [ a -&gt; let b n-common + a * n-uniq
    foreach range n-uniq [ i -&gt; foreach range i [ j -&gt; set pairs lput (list (b + j) (b + i)) pairs set owner lput a owner ] ] ]
  let lo (ifelse-value processing-skill = "high" [ 3 ] processing-skill = "moderate" [ 6 ] [ 9 ])
  create-turtles 3 [ set enc lo + random 3  set dec enc + 1  hide-turtle
    set dprog n-values 36 [ 0 ]  set info n-values length pairs [ 0 ]  set said n-values length pairs [ false ] ]
  let ranked sort-on [ enc ] turtles
  ask turtles [ set speak 1 ]
  if communication = "slowest learner speaks twice as often" [ ask last ranked [ set speak 2 ] ]
  if communication = "fastest learner speaks twice as often" [ ask first ranked [ set speak 2 ] ]
  set phase "learning" set clock 0 set done-at 0
  ask turtles [ set order shuffle my-data ]
  draw reset-ticks
end

to-report my-data  report sentence range n-common (n-values n-uniq [ i -&gt; n-common + who * n-uniq + i ]) end
to-report done? [ d ]  report item d dprog &gt;= enc end
to-report learned? [ k ]  report item k info &gt;= dec end

to learn  ;; one learning action
  let ready filter [ k -&gt; (item k owner = -1 or item k owner = who) and not learned? k
                          and done? first item k pairs and done? last item k pairs ] range length pairs
  ifelse not empty? ready [ set info replace-item (first ready) info dec ]          ;; integrate a pair
  [ set order filter [ d -&gt; not done? d ] order
    if not empty? order [ let d first order  set dprog replace-item d dprog (item d dprog + 1) ] ]
end

to-report eligible  report filter [ k -&gt; learned? k and not all? turtles [ item k said ] ] range length pairs end

to share  ;; one sharing time step
  let candidates turtles with [ not empty? eligible ]
  if not any? candidates [ set clock 50 stop ]
  let r random-float sum [ speak ] of candidates
  let speaker nobody
  foreach sort candidates [ t -&gt; if speaker = nobody [ set r r - [speak] of t  if r &lt; 0 [ set speaker t ] ] ]
  if speaker = nobody [ set speaker one-of candidates ]
  let k one-of [ eligible ] of speaker
  ask speaker [ set said replace-item k said true ]
  ask turtles [ if not learned? k [ set info replace-item k info (item k info + 1) ] ]   ;; decoding attempt
end

to go
  if done-at &gt; 0 [ stop ]
  ifelse phase = "learning" [ ask turtles [ learn ] ] [ share ]
  set clock clock + 1
  if clock &gt;= 50 [
    set clock 0
    ifelse phase = "learning" [ set phase "sharing" ]
      [ if any? turtles with [ not empty? filter [ d -&gt; not done? d ] my-data or
                               not empty? filter [ k -&gt; (item k owner = -1 or item k owner = who) and not learned? k ] range length pairs ]
          [ set phase "learning" ask turtles [ set order shuffle my-data ] ] ] ]
  tick
  if all? turtles [ length eligible = 0 and min info &gt;= dec ] and all? turtles [ reduce and said ] [ set done-at ticks ]
  draw
end

to-report pct-learned-by-all report 100 * length filter [ k -&gt; all? turtles [ learned? k ] ] range length pairs / length pairs end
to-report pct-said-by-all report 100 * length filter [ k -&gt; all? turtles [ item k said ] ] range length pairs / length pairs end

to draw  ;; display only: one panel per member; light gray = not learned, dark gray = learned, red "+" = said
  ask patches [ set pcolor [242 242 242] set plabel "" ]
  foreach sort turtles [ t -&gt; foreach range length pairs [ k -&gt;
    ask patch ([who] of t * 17 - 25 + k mod 15) (10 - floor (k / 15)) [
      set pcolor ifelse-value [item k said] of t [ [182 0 0] ] [ ifelse-value [learned? k] of t [ [51 51 51] ] [ [225 225 225] ] ]
      if [item k said] of t [ set plabel "+" set plabel-color white ] ] ] ]
end
</code>
  <widgets>
    <view x="360" wrappingAllowedX="false" y="10" frameRate="30.0" minPycor="-10" height="294" showTickCounter="true" patchSize="14" fontSize="14" wrappingAllowedY="false" width="714" tickCounterLabel="time steps" maxPycor="10" updateMode="1" maxPxcor="25" minPxcor="-25"></view>
    <button x="10" y="10" height="40" disableUntilTicks="false" forever="false" kind="Observer" width="110" display="setup">setup</button>
    <button x="130" y="10" height="40" disableUntilTicks="true" forever="true" kind="Observer" width="110" display="go">go</button>
    <chooser x="10" y="60" height="60" variable="processing-skill" current="1" width="330" display="processing-skill"><choice type="string" value="high"></choice><choice type="string" value="moderate"></choice><choice type="string" value="low"></choice></chooser>
    <chooser x="10" y="130" height="60" variable="communication" current="1" width="330" display="communication"><choice type="string" value="slowest learner speaks twice as often"></choice><choice type="string" value="all members equally"></choice><choice type="string" value="fastest learner speaks twice as often"></choice></chooser>
    <chooser x="10" y="200" height="60" variable="specialization" current="2" width="330" display="specialization"><choice type="string" value="low (33% unique)"></choice><choice type="string" value="moderate (50% unique)"></choice><choice type="string" value="high (66% unique)"></choice></chooser>
    <monitor x="10" precision="0" y="270" height="60" fontSize="14" width="160" display="phase">phase</monitor>
    <monitor x="180" precision="0" y="270" height="60" fontSize="14" width="160" display="time steps to finish">done-at</monitor>
    <plot x="10" autoPlotX="true" yMax="100" autoPlotY="false" yAxis="% of pool" y="340" xMin="0.0" height="250" legend="true" xMax="200" yMin="0" width="330" xAxis="time step" display="Team knowledge over time"><setup></setup><update></update><pen interval="1.0" mode="0" display="learned by all" color="-13421773" legend="true"><setup></setup><update>plot pct-learned-by-all</update></pen><pen interval="1.0" mode="0" display="stated by all" color="-4849664" legend="true"><setup></setup><update>plot pct-said-by-all</update></pen></plot>
  </widgets>
  <info><![CDATA[## WHAT IS IT?

Presenter implementation of the team knowledge emergence model of Grand, Braun, Kuljanin, Kozlowski, and Chao (2016). Three agents alternate 50-step learning phases (encode their own data, then integrate pairs of learned data into information) and 50-step sharing phases (one speaker per step states a random piece of information they have learned that not every member has yet stated; every member who has not yet learned it makes one decoding attempt).

## DISPLAY

One panel per member; each cell is one piece of information (a pair of data). Light gray = not learned; dark gray = learned; red with a plus sign = this member has stated it to the team.

## SOURCES AND DIFFERENCES

Structure follows the paper's Table A1/A2 and the authors' supplementary R code (APL-2014-0766R3_Supp.R.txt). Speaking probabilities follow the paper's text (favored member twice as likely, 50/25/25); the R code uses 60/20/20. Like the R code, there is no separate acknowledgment step: a member's statement of an item counts as that member's externalization. The run ends when every member has learned every piece and every member has stated every piece.

Grand, J. A., Braun, M. T., Kuljanin, G., Kozlowski, S. W. J., & Chao, G. T. (2016). The dynamics of team cognition: A process-oriented theory of knowledge emergence in teams. Journal of Applied Psychology, 101(10), 1353-1385.
]]></info>
